A Data Principal must:

- Comply with all applicable laws while exercising rights under this Act;  
- Not impersonate another person when providing personal data for a specified purpose;  
- Not suppress any material information when providing personal data for any document, unique identifier, proof of identity or proof of address issued by the State or its instrumentalities;  
- Not register a false or frivolous grievance or complaint with a Data Fiduciary or the Board; and  
- Furnish only verifiably authentic information when exercising the right to correction or erasure.  

[Section 15]
